737281 748400513  4096 Oct 22 23:27 workspace\\n---ls /home---\\ntotal 0\\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 1776737281 748400513  60 Oct 22 23:27 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x 12 1776737281 748400513 240 Oct 22 23:27 ..\\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 1776737281 748400513  40 Oct 22 23:27 actor\\n---ls /root---\\n\", \"output_truncated\": false}"}], "is_error": false, "kind": "BenchmarkObservation"}, "action_id": "abb34cb0-f8aa-43d0-9579-7de088c17fed", "extended_content": [], "kind": "ObservationEvent", "source_event_index": 8}
{"id": "c7033b6c-0454-444c-bba4-bc49e59e08b2", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T16:27:42.576999", "source": "environment", "parent_id": "e2361819-8d4a-40bb-b03b-aab2b2c97aa9", "tool_name": "execute_check", "tool_call_id": "call-35736af4-f1c8-447f-b084-f1d04a345bc7", "observation": {"content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"phase\": \"exploration\", \"command\": \"echo '---track.md search---' ; find / -maxdepth 4 -name 'track.md' 2>/dev/null ; echo '---disk---' ; df -h 2>&1 | head -10 ; echo '---memory---' ; free -h 2>&1 | head -5 ; echo '---python---' ; python3 --version 2>&1 ; echo '---nvidia---' ; nvidia-smi 2>&1 | head -5 ; echo '---pip packages (sample)---' ; pip3 list 2>/dev/null | grep -iE 'torch|transformers|datasets|huggingface|accelerate|numpy|scipy' | head -30\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"timed_out\": false, \"elapsed_seconds\": 0.315, \"output\": \"---track.md search---\\n---disk---\\nFilesystem                         Size  Used Avail Use% Mounted on\\ntmpfs                               63G     0   63G   0% /\\n/dev/mapper/ubuntu--vg-ubuntu--lv  1.8T 1017G  710G  59% /usr\\ntmpfs                               63G     0   63G   0% /dev\\ntmpfs                               63G     0   63G   0% /tmp\\n---memory---\\n               total        used        free      shared  buff/cache   available\\nMem:           125Gi        21Gi       9.9Gi       128Mi        94Gi       103Gi\\nSwap:           61Gi       1.8Gi        60Gi\\n---python---\\nPython 3.12.3\\n---nvidia---\\nNVIDIA-SMI has failed because it couldn't communicate with the NVIDIA driver. Make sure that the latest NVIDIA driver is installed and running.\\n\\n---pip packages (sample)---\\n\", \"output_truncated\": false}"}], "is_error": false, "kind": "BenchmarkObservation"}, "action_id": "3f0f70b1-8ab6-4b8c-a5f0-8bc3b0ddf8aa", "extended_content": [], "kind": "ObservationEvent", "source_event_index": 9}
{"id": "7fe6e348-9cbb-4f21-8e96-5843c8eccfb4", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T16:29:39.555900", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "c7033b6c-0454-444c-bba4-bc49e59e08b2", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-189ae362-d1e2-4fa7-90a0-ea3771709037", "tool_call": {"id": "call-189ae362-d1e2-4fa7-90a0-ea3771709037", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\":\"Submit plan proposal for review\",\"stage\":\"plan\",\"answer\":\"PROPOSED EXPERIMENT DESIGN (PLAN STAGE). No experiments run; runtime is design-only and confirms workspace contains only task.json with no starter code, no model weights, no datasets, and no GPU. Below is the proposed approach, awaiting researcher approval before the final design write-up.\\n\\n1) Repository / input inspection\\n- /workspace contains only task.json (574 B), which in turn carries a documents.track.md field whose value is the literal string \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\" There is no track.md on disk.\\n- /home/actor is empty; no README, .py files, configs, weight pointers, or eval scripts anywhere under /workspace, /home, /root, /tmp.\\n- Environment: Python 3.12.3, NO torch/transformers/datasets/accelerate installed, nvidia-smi indicates no GPU, 24 CPU cores, 125 GiB RAM, ~710 GiB free disk.\\n- Relevance: nothing in the workspace is directly reusable. The final design must be reconstructed entirely from the locked requirements (LLAMA2-7B, symmetric input, asymmetric KV-cache, PPL, clipping-ratio IV) and publicly referenced PTQ/LLM-quantization methodology.\\n\\n2) Proposed approach (seven sub-items)\\n(i) Sweep over clipping ratios: define ξ ∈ (0,1] as the operational scalar; sweep bounds [0.30, 1.00] with a log-uniform 13-point primary grid {0.30, 0.40, 0.50, 0.60, 0.65, 0.70, 0.75, 0.80, 0.85, 0.90, 0.95, 0.99, 1.00} plus local 3-point refinement around the candidate optimum (rarefying until per-step ΔPPL < 0.02). Justification: log spacing reflects that clipping-error variance scales with (1−ξ)² near 1 and rounding-error variance with ξ⁻² near 0, so the U-shaped E_total curve is best resolved on a log axis; literature anchors (SmoothQuant α∈[0.3,0.7], GPTQ 0.7–0.95) put the plausible optimum in [0.6,0.95].\\n(ii) Operational definition of clipping ratio for symmetric input quantization: τ = ξ · M where M = max|x| over the chosen scope; scale s = τ/127; X̂ = round(clamp(X,−τ,+τ)/s)·s. Scope fixed at per-token, symmetric INT8, single global ξ across all transformer blocks. Justification: per-tensor is too outlier-sensitive for LLaMA-family (typical PPL inflation +1–3 at INT8); per-token matches the SmoothQuant/INT8 cuBLAS-CUTLASS convention; per-channel is technically richer but makes the IV a vector and is out of scope for a single scalar ratio question.\\n(iii) Asymmetric KV-cache quantization: INT8, per-token, per-head granularity (group size = head_dim = 128). Asymmetric mapping: s = (max−min)/255, z = round(−min/s), codes ∈ [0,255]. Statistics computed dynamically per token per head at runtime — no offline KV calibration. Same scalar ξ acts at the KV site as ξ on max|K| in K and ξ on (max V − min V) in V around the asymmetric (min,max) quantizer.\\n(iv) Evaluation protocol: PPL primary; datasets WikiText-2 raw test (≈287.6K tokens) + C4 en validation (256 sequences × 2048 tokens); PTB optional diagnostic. Context length 2048, stride 2048, greedy decoding, FP32 master weights, INT8 KV-cache. Calibration set: 16 × 2048 tokens from C4 en train (disjoint from both eval splits). Baselines: (a) FP16 floor; (b) ξ=1.0 (no-clip saturation); (c) percentile-99.5 reference (the canonical adaptive calibration); (d) MSE-optimal oracle upper bound.\\n(v) Controls and ablations: C1 granularity ablation (per-tensor, per-token, per-channel); C2 with/without KV quantization; C3 symmetric vs. asymmetric KV; C4 attention-only vs. MLP-only ξ application; C5 offline-max vs. dynamic-max; C6 seed sensitivity (3 seeds); C7 context-length sensitivity {1024, 2048, 4096}; C8 SmoothQuant-style α=0.5 rebalanced sweep. C1, C2, C5 mandatory; others recommended under compute.\\n(vi) Analysis plan: (a) PPL(ξ) on log-x with markers for FP16, ξ=1.0, percentile; (b) ΔPPL(ξ) and PPL/PPL(FP16); (c) per-layer error decomposition E_clip(τ)/var(x) and E_round(τ)/var(x) for bias–variance story; (d) layer-provenance plot of E_clip vs. ΔPPL; (e) ξ* ± robustness half-width where |PPL(ξ)−min PPL| ≤ 0.05; (f) gap to percentile and oracle baselines; (g) bootstrap 95% CI over evaluation windows for top three ξ candidates.\\n(vii) Feasibility: on-paper, fully deliverable with zero compute, weights, datasets, or GPU here — outputs are the design document plus mockable analysis figures. If execution were in scope: FP16 LLAMA2-7B ≈ 14 GB; activations ≈ 1 GB at seq 2048; KV-cache FP16 ≈ 1.0 GB → INT8 ≈ 0.5 GB → total resident < 20 GB → fits a 24 GB GPU. Per-eval point ≈ 2.5 min on RTX 3090; 16 points × 2 datasets × 4 cells ≈ 12–16 GPU-hours on a 3090, < 6 hours on A100. Stack: transformers, accelerate, datasets, torch≥2.1, bitsandbytes INT8 linear with custom per-token activation hook, plus a custom attention path for INT8 K/V pre-step + FP16 logits (KIVI/KVQuant-style). CONCLUSION: out of scope for THIS task; design-only per the brief.\\n\\n3) Consequential assumptions and uncertainties\\nAssumptions (would be locked in for the final design):\\n- A1 Symmetric input quantization = per-token, INT8, single global ξ across all blocks.\\n- A2 max|x| computed dynamically per token at runtime (not offline).\\n- A3 KV-cache = per-token, per-head, INT8 (group = head_dim = 128).\\n- A4 KV min/max computed dynamically per token per head.\\n- A5 ξ acts at KV sites as ξ·max|K| in K and ξ·(max V − min V) in V around the asymmetric (min,max) quantizer.\\n- A6 Sweep: log-uniform 13 points {0.30, 0.40, 0.50, 0.60, 0.65, 0.70, 0.75, 0.80, 0.85, 0.90, 0.95, 0.99, 1.00} + local 3-point refinement.\\n- A7 PPL on WikiText-2 raw + C4 en validation (256 × 2048 tokens); PTB optional.\\n- A8 Context 2048, stride 2048, greedy, FP16 master weights.\\n- A9 Calibration: 16 × 2048 tokens from C4 en train, disjoint from eval splits; used only by the percentile baseline and C5.\\n- A10 \\\"Best ratio\\\" = argmin PPL on WikiText-2 (primary) with C4 as generalization check; report robust region |PPL−min PPL| ≤ 0.05.\\n- A11 Baselines: FP16, ξ=1.0, percentile-99.5, MSE-oracle.\\n- A12 Weights stay FP16 (the brief does not specify weight quant; reducing weight precision widens the rounding-error floor and is out of scope unless requested).\\n\\nUncertainties that could materially change the recommended ξ*:\\n- U1 Layer heterogeneity — early-attention vs. late-MLP outliers in LLaMA2 differ; a global scalar may compromise by 0.05–0.10.\\n- U2 Granularity interaction — per-channel input quant shifts ξ* upward by 0.05–0.15 vs. per-token. Our per-token choice is conservative; if the user prefers per-channel the design replans the sweep.\\n- U3 KV-cache bit-width — the brief is silent on bits; INT4 KV couples Kᵀ·Q rounding error with input clipping and could shift ξ* by 0.05–0.10 or even shadow the input effect. We assume INT8.\\n- U4 Calibration strategy — offline vs. dynamic per-token max can change M by 5–15% on LLaMA models, shifting ξ*. C5 control mitigates.\\n- U5 SmoothQuant-style α rebalancing — per-channel scaling changes the effective dynamic range; ξ* moves non-trivially. We add C8 as an optional rerun.\\n- U6 Context length — KV error accumulates with T; T=4096 can move ξ* up to ~0.05 vs. T=2048. C7 sweep probes this.\\n- U7 Weight precision — INT4/INT8 weights widen the rounding floor and shift ξ*; we lock FP16 weights unless told otherwise.\\n- U8 Attention-precision impl — INT8 K/V dequantized to FP16 vs. integer accumulation + FP32 accumulator can flip ΔPPL by 0.1–0.3. We fix the FP16-dequant path.\\n- U9 Dataset-shift sensitivity — WikiText-2 and C4 may disagree on ξ* by >0.05 for LL