tions and uncertainties\\nAssumptions (would be locked in for the final design):\\n- A1 Symmetric input quantization = per-token, INT8, single global \\u03be across all blocks.\\n- A2 max|x| computed dynamically per token at runtime (not offline).\\n- A3 KV-cache = per-token, per-head, INT8 (group = head_dim = 128).\\n- A4 KV min/max computed dynamically per token per head.\\n- A5 \\u03be acts at KV sites as \\u03be\\u00b7max|K| in K and \\u03be\\u00b7(max V \\u2212 min V) in V around the asymmetric (min,max) quantizer.\\n- A6 Sweep: log-uniform 13 points {0.30, 0.40, 0.50, 0.60, 0.65, 0.70, 0.75, 0.80, 0.85, 0.90, 0.95, 0.99, 1.00} + local 3-point refinement.\\n- A7 PPL on WikiText-2 raw + C4 en validation (256 \\u00d7 2048 tokens); PTB optional.\\n- A8 Context 2048, stride 2048, greedy, FP16 master weights.\\n- A9 Calibration: 16 \\u00d7 2048 tokens from C4 en train, disjoint from eval splits; used only by the percentile baseline and C5.\\n- A10 \\\"Best ratio\\\" = argmin PPL on WikiText-2 (primary) with C4 as generalization check; report robust region |PPL\\u2212min PPL| \\u2264 0.05.\\n- A11 Baselines: FP16, \\u03be=1.0, percentile-99.5, MSE-oracle.\\n- A12 Weights stay FP16 (the brief does not specify weight quant; reducing weight precision widens the rounding-error floor and is out of scope unless requested).\\n\\nUncertainties that could materially change the recommended \\u03be*:\\n- U1 Layer heterogeneity \\u2014 early-attention vs. late-MLP outliers in LLaMA2 differ; a global scalar may compromise by 0.05\\u20130.10.\\n- U2 Per-channel activation granularity would shift \\u03be* upward by 0.05\\u20130.15 vs. per-token.\\n- U3 KV-cache bit-width is unspecified \\u2014 INT4 KV couples K\\u1d40\\u00b7Q error with input clipping; could shadow or shift the optimum.\\n- U4 Calibration strategy (offline vs. dynamic per-token max) changes M by 5\\u201315% on LLaMA-family; can shift \\u03be*.\\n- U5 SmoothQuant-style \\u03b1 rebalancing changes effective dynamic range; \\u03be* moves non-trivially (C8).\\n- U6 Context length \\u2014 KV error accumulates with T; at T=4096 \\u03be* may differ by up to ~0.05 vs. T=2048.\\n- U7 Weight precision (W4A8, W8A8 vs. FP16 weights) widens rounding-error floor and shifts \\u03be*.\\n- U8 Attention-precision impl (FP16 dequant vs. integer accumulation + FP32) can flip \\u0394PPL by 0.1\\u20130.3.\\n- U9 WikiText-2 vs. C4 PPL may disagree on \\u03be* by >0.05; we must report both rather than average.\\n\\nEnd of plan; please confirm or request changes before I proceed to stage=result.\", \"evidence\": \"Inspection performed via execute_check: (a) `ls -la /workspace` returns one entry `task.json`; (b) `find /workspace -maxdepth 3 -type f | wc -l` returns 1; (c) `cat /workspace/task.json` shows the question plus `documents.track.md == \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\"`, and no `track.md` exists on disk anywhere under the standard search paths; (d) `/home/actor` is empty; (e) `nvidia-smi` returns \\\"couldn't communicate with the NVIDIA driver\\\" \\u2192 no GPU; (f) `pip3 list | grep -iE 'torch|transformers|datasets|huggingface|accelerate|numpy|scipy'` returns no entries \\u2192 no ML stack installed; (g) system reports Python 3.12.3, 24 CPUs, 125 GiB RAM, ~710 GiB free disk. All design choices are inferred from the locked requirements and PTQ literature; no external assets or pre-existing code consulted.\", \"assumptions\": [\"A1 Symmetric input quantization = per-token, INT8, single global \\u03be across all transformer blocks.\", \"A2 max|x| computed dynamically per token at runtime (not offline).\", \"A3 KV-cache = per-token, per-head, INT8 (group size = head_dim = 128).\", \"A4 KV min/max computed dynamically per token per head.\", \"A5 \\u03be acts at KV sites as \\u03be\\u00b7max|K| in K and \\u03be\\u00b7(max V \\u2212 min V) in V around the asymmetric (min,max) quantizer.\", \"A6 Sweep: log-uniform 13 points {0.30, 0.40, 0.50, 0.60, 0.65, 0.70, 0.75, 0.80, 0.85, 0.90, 0.95, 0.99, 1.00} + local 3-point refinement.\", \"A7 PPL on WikiText-2 raw + C4 en validation (256 \\u00d7 2048 tokens); PTB optional diagnostic.\", \"A8 Context length 2048, stride 2048, greedy decoding, FP16 master weights.\", \"A9 Calibration set: 16 \\u00d7 2048 tokens from C4 en train, disjoint from both eval splits.\", \"A10 \\\"Best ratio\\\" = argmin PPL on WikiText-2 with C4 generalization check; report robust region |PPL\\u2212min PPL| \\u2264 0.05.\", \"A11 Baselines: FP16, \\u03be=1.0, percentile-99.5, MSE-oracle.\", \"A12 Weights stay FP16 (brief does not specify weight quant; reducing weight precision is out of scope unless requested).\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"U1 Layer heterogeneity \\u2014 early-attention vs. late-MLP outliers differ in LLaMA-family; a global scalar may compromise \\u03be* by 0.05\\u20130.10.\", \"U2 Per-channel activation granularity would shift \\u03be* upward by 0.05\\u20130.15 vs. per-token.\", \"U3 KV-cache bit-width is unspecified \\u2014 INT4 KV couples K\\u1d40\\u00b7Q error with input clipping; could shadow or shift the optimum.\", \"U4 Calibration strategy (offline vs. dynamic per-token max) changes M by 5\\u201315% on LLaMA-family; can shift \\u03be*.\", \"U5 SmoothQuant-style \\u03b1 rebalancing changes the effective dynamic range; \\u03be* moves non-trivially (C8).\", \"U6 Context length \\u2014 KV error accumulates with T; at T=4096 \\u03be* may differ by up to ~0.05 vs. T=2048.\", \"U7 Weight precision (W4A8 / W8A8 vs. FP16 weights) widens the rounding-error floor and shifts \\u03be*.\", \"U8 Attention-precision impl (FP16 dequant vs. integer accumulation + FP32) can flip \\u0394PPL by 0.1\\u20130.3.\", \"U9 WikiText-2 vs. C4 PPL may disagree on \\u03be* by >0.05; we will report both rather than average.\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-dee50b17-cec1-49e3-b3d3-760e8f14ecb0", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 12}
